title: "xdp-guard: A Memory-Safe, Line-Rate In-Kernel Firewall and Volumetric DDoS Mitigation Engine in Pure Rust via eBPF/XDP"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
url: "https://github.com/rahadbhuiya/xdp-guard"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahadbhuiya/xdp-guard"
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - ebpf
  - xdp
  - rust
  - aya
  - sched-ext
  - ddos-mitigation
  - linux-kernel
  - rate-limiting
abstract: "xdp-guard is an in-kernel packet filter and rate-limiting engine written strictly in pure Rust using the Aya eBPF framework. Executing at the network device driver level via XDP, it enforces line-rate deterministic drops prior to OS socket buffer allocations, incorporating in-kernel token-bucket rate limiting and empirical resilience against adversarial burst flooding under Linux 6.12 sched_ext schedulers."
